WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.234 --> 00:00:02.401
-Hi, everybody,
welcome, welcome, welcome

00:00:02.401 --> 00:00:04.737
to "The Tonight Show"!
Here we go.

00:00:04.737 --> 00:00:06.172
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:06.172 --> 00:00:08.474
Thank you so much for being
here, thank you for watching.

00:00:08.474 --> 00:00:10.009
Now let's
get to the news and jokes.

00:00:10.009 --> 00:00:12.111
Well, guys,
everybody is talking about this.

00:00:12.111 --> 00:00:14.914
On Sunday, President Trump
announced over Twitter

00:00:14.914 --> 00:00:18.918
that Rudy Giuliani
tested positive for coronavirus.

00:00:18.918 --> 00:00:21.020
When the news broke,
the coronavirus was like,

00:00:21.020 --> 00:00:22.555
"Damn it! I knew
I should have worn a mask!"

00:00:22.555 --> 00:00:24.890
[ Laughter ]

00:00:24.890 --> 00:00:26.159
I hope Rudy's okay.

00:00:26.159 --> 00:00:28.728
When they did his nasal swab,
it came out black.

00:00:28.728 --> 00:00:32.331
[ Laughter ]

00:00:32.331 --> 00:00:33.633
Apparently, the doctor asked,

00:00:33.633 --> 00:00:35.267
"When did you start
feeling a little off?"

00:00:35.267 --> 00:00:38.304
And Rudy said,
"Right around 2009-ish."

00:00:38.304 --> 00:00:40.340
[ Laughter ]

00:00:40.340 --> 00:00:42.008
It keeps getting worse for Rudy.

00:00:42.008 --> 00:00:44.009
After his test
showed he had COVID,

00:00:44.009 --> 00:00:45.912
he challenged the results
in court and lost.

00:00:45.912 --> 00:00:49.282
[ Laughter ]

00:00:49.282 --> 00:00:50.883
Rudy was like,
"How could this happen?

00:00:50.883 --> 00:00:52.718
All I did
was travel around maskless

00:00:52.718 --> 00:00:55.288
and use whatever I found laying
around to wipe my face."

00:00:55.288 --> 00:00:56.989
[ Laughter ]

00:00:56.989 --> 00:00:59.225
At first, it was hard to tell
that Rudy had COVID

00:00:59.225 --> 00:01:01.628
'cause he always looked like
he had a 102-degree fever.

00:01:01.628 --> 00:01:02.828
[ Laughter ]

00:01:02.828 --> 00:01:04.897
Well, the good news is,
Giuliani already tweeted

00:01:04.897 --> 00:01:07.800
that he is getting great care
and feeling good.

00:01:07.800 --> 00:01:10.904
Yep, nurses have been giving him
I.V. fluids,

00:01:10.904 --> 00:01:12.971
which Rudy promptly
sprays out of his face

00:01:12.971 --> 00:01:14.107
like a lawn sprinkler.

00:01:14.107 --> 00:01:16.376
[ Laughter ]

00:01:16.376 --> 00:01:17.677
I hope Rudy's getting good care,

00:01:17.677 --> 00:01:19.211
because if he picks
medical experts

00:01:19.211 --> 00:01:22.148
like he picks legal experts,
his doctor is gonna be

00:01:22.148 --> 00:01:24.751
some random guy he found
at an Applebee's happy hour.

00:01:24.751 --> 00:01:26.252
[ Laughter ]

00:01:26.252 --> 00:01:28.420
Yeah, Rudy says he's feeling
good and will be back

00:01:28.420 --> 00:01:31.657
to embarrassing himself
on camera in no time.

00:01:31.657 --> 00:01:34.794
-Hang on! Wait a minute.
Did you say Giuliani got COVID?

00:01:34.794 --> 00:01:37.397
-Yeah. Yeah,
that's what I've been saying.

00:01:37.397 --> 00:01:39.432
-Giuliani Bingo!

00:01:39.432 --> 00:01:41.000
-No way!
You got Giuliani Bingo?

00:01:41.000 --> 00:01:43.670
-Yeah, man.
Giuliani Bingo.

00:01:43.670 --> 00:01:45.838
-All right.
Let's double-check your card.

00:01:45.838 --> 00:01:48.007
You got Giuliani
testing positive for COVID.

00:01:48.007 --> 00:01:49.809
What else?
-Well, I've got

00:01:49.809 --> 00:01:52.445
"Audibly farted
during a hearing."

00:01:52.445 --> 00:01:54.013
-They didn't bother to interview
a single witness.

00:01:54.013 --> 00:01:55.014
[ Farts ]

00:01:55.014 --> 00:01:56.749
-Oh, well, I have...

00:01:56.749 --> 00:02:00.486
"Brought a lady to court
who seemed to be drunk."

00:02:00.486 --> 00:02:04.156
-The poll bo-- The poll book
is completely off.

00:02:04.156 --> 00:02:06.659
-I have
"Wiped his face with a rag

00:02:06.659 --> 00:02:09.261
that he just
blew his nose into."

00:02:09.261 --> 00:02:11.097
-That is true.

00:02:11.097 --> 00:02:12.498
[ Laughter ]

00:02:12.498 --> 00:02:16.235
-And, finally,
"Hair dye melted off his face."

00:02:16.235 --> 00:02:17.669
Giuliani Bingo, man.

00:02:17.669 --> 00:02:20.973
-Yeah. You won. Tariq,
you've got one Giuliani Bingo!

00:02:20.973 --> 00:02:22.475
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:22.475 --> 00:02:23.476
♪♪

00:02:23.476 --> 00:02:26.312
Your prize is a $25 gift card

00:02:26.312 --> 00:02:29.148
to Four Seasons
Total Landscaping. Congrats.

00:02:29.148 --> 00:02:33.452
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:33.452 --> 00:02:34.888
Meanwhile,
all eyes are on Georgia

00:02:34.888 --> 00:02:36.422
and its two Senate runoffs.

00:02:36.422 --> 00:02:38.057
On Saturday, Trump held a rally

00:02:38.057 --> 00:02:40.226
for the state's
Republican Senators,

00:02:40.226 --> 00:02:42.261
but he mostly
talked about himself.

00:02:42.261 --> 00:02:45.031
Here he is complaining
about his own election results.

00:02:45.031 --> 00:02:46.832
-We're all victims.
Everybody here,

00:02:46.832 --> 00:02:49.268
all these thousands of people
here tonight,

00:02:49.268 --> 00:02:51.303
they're all victims.
Every one of you.

00:02:51.303 --> 00:02:54.506
-Yeah. And judging by the number
of masks I saw in the crowd,

00:02:54.506 --> 00:02:56.876
he's right.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:56.876 --> 00:02:59.612
Even Rudy Giuliani saw that
and said, "You fools!"

00:02:59.612 --> 00:03:04.684
[ Laughter ]

00:03:04.684 --> 00:03:05.785
"You fools!"

00:03:05.785 --> 00:03:07.086
[ Laughter ]

00:03:07.086 --> 00:03:09.421
But in the end, Trump knows
there's a lot on the line

00:03:09.421 --> 00:03:11.824
in Georgia, so he made sure
to deliver a compelling

00:03:11.824 --> 00:03:14.327
closing argument
for the Republican candidates.

00:03:14.327 --> 00:03:15.094
Watch.

00:03:15.094 --> 00:03:18.331
♪♪

00:03:18.331 --> 00:03:21.633
-Blueberries, peppers,
squash, and cucumbers.

00:03:21.633 --> 00:03:23.969
Who does cucumbers around here?

00:03:23.969 --> 00:03:26.605
'Cause I like cucumbers!
I'm the only one.

00:03:26.605 --> 00:03:28.040
I like cucumbers.

00:03:28.040 --> 00:03:31.177
♪♪

00:03:31.177 --> 00:03:33.579
[ Applause ]

00:03:33.579 --> 00:03:35.481
-Well, last night,
there was supposed to be

00:03:35.481 --> 00:03:39.152
a debate for Georgia's runoff
between Democrat John Ossoff

00:03:39.152 --> 00:03:40.953
and Republican David Perdue,

00:03:40.953 --> 00:03:44.423
but Perdue didn't show up,
so look what happened.

00:03:44.423 --> 00:03:49.161
-Democrat John Ossoff.
He is CEO of Insight TWI,

00:03:49.161 --> 00:03:51.697
a media production company
that investigates corruption,

00:03:51.697 --> 00:03:53.666
organized crime, and war crimes

00:03:53.666 --> 00:03:56.102
for international
news organizations.

00:03:56.102 --> 00:03:57.369
Republican David Perdue

00:03:57.369 --> 00:03:59.906
has served
in the U.S. Senate since 2015.

00:03:59.906 --> 00:04:03.209
Senator Perdue declined
to participate in this debate

00:04:03.209 --> 00:04:05.578
and is represented
by an empty podium.

00:04:05.578 --> 00:04:09.115
[ Laughter ]

00:04:09.115 --> 00:04:10.916
-Afterward,
the podium was kicking itself,

00:04:10.916 --> 00:04:12.818
was like, "I blew it.
I totally froze.

00:04:12.818 --> 00:04:14.354
I just..."
[ Laughter ]

00:04:14.354 --> 00:04:15.955
Yeah, it was a rough night
for the podium.

00:04:15.955 --> 00:04:18.390
Halfway through the debate,
a fly landed on it.

00:04:18.390 --> 00:04:21.361
[ Laughter ]
Unbelievable, unbelievable.

00:04:21.361 --> 00:04:22.861
Meanwhile,
today, at the White House,

00:04:22.861 --> 00:04:24.596
Trump gave the Medal of Freedom

00:04:24.596 --> 00:04:26.866
to a legendary wrestling coach
from Iowa.

00:04:26.866 --> 00:04:29.101
But listen to what he said
at the ceremony.

00:04:29.101 --> 00:04:34.640
-He won 117 consecutive matches
and lost only one.

00:04:34.640 --> 00:04:40.013
Well, you know, in politics,
I won two, so I'm 2-0,

00:04:40.013 --> 00:04:42.114
and that's pretty good, too.

00:04:42.114 --> 00:04:43.816
But we'll see
how that turns out.

00:04:43.816 --> 00:04:45.817
[ Laughter ]

00:04:45.817 --> 00:04:47.720
-At that point, Trump took back
the Medal of Freedom

00:04:47.720 --> 00:04:48.921
and gave it to himself.

00:04:48.921 --> 00:04:53.159
"I'm undefeated,
and you're not, so..."

00:04:53.159 --> 00:04:55.594
Trump's 2-0 claim
would've been more convincing

00:04:55.594 --> 00:04:58.431
if half the people in that room
weren't moving guys.

00:04:58.431 --> 00:04:59.965
"All right.
We gotta get this thing.

00:04:59.965 --> 00:05:02.167
You want to go diagonal
with this through the door?

00:05:02.167 --> 00:05:05.638
Yeah."
[ Laughter ]

00:05:05.638 --> 00:05:07.974
Here's some music news --
Bob Dylan just sold

00:05:07.974 --> 00:05:10.976
his entire songwriting catalog
to Universal

00:05:10.976 --> 00:05:13.379
in a giant,
record-breaking deal.

00:05:13.379 --> 00:05:15.147
I'm thrilled for Bob Dylan,
but if I see

00:05:15.147 --> 00:05:17.316
"Blowin' in the Wind"
in a Gas-X commercial,

00:05:17.316 --> 00:05:20.152
I'm gonna freak out.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:20.152 --> 00:05:21.353
No.

00:05:21.353 --> 00:05:23.222
That's right.
Bob Dylan just sold his entire

00:05:23.222 --> 00:05:27.259
music catalog for over
an estimated $300 million.

00:05:27.259 --> 00:05:29.728
It's one of the biggest music
publishing deals ever.

00:05:29.728 --> 00:05:32.264
And this is real --
here now, on the phone,

00:05:32.264 --> 00:05:35.301
to talk about this enormous deal
is Bob Dylan himself.

00:05:35.301 --> 00:05:37.302
Bob, are you there?

00:05:37.302 --> 00:05:41.240
-[ Speaking indistinctly ]

00:05:41.240 --> 00:05:45.411
Okay. Well, how do you feel
about this record-breaking deal?

00:05:45.411 --> 00:05:51.550
-[ Speaking indistinctly ]

00:05:51.550 --> 00:05:53.886
-I see, I see.
And how do you plan

00:05:53.886 --> 00:05:55.587
to spend all of that money?

00:05:55.587 --> 00:06:00.426
-[ Speaking indistinctly ]

00:06:00.426 --> 00:06:01.827
...PlayStation 5.

00:06:01.827 --> 00:06:03.929
-Uh-huh.
That's really great.

00:06:03.929 --> 00:06:06.532
Well, I know you're hoping to
debut a new song here tonight.

00:06:06.532 --> 00:06:09.669
So, please, take it away,
whenever you're ready.

00:06:09.669 --> 00:06:11.737
-One, two...

00:06:11.737 --> 00:06:13.906
[ Singing indistinctly ]

00:06:13.906 --> 00:06:23.916
♪♪

00:06:23.916 --> 00:06:26.118
♪♪

00:06:26.118 --> 00:06:27.720
♪ PlayStation 5 ♪

00:06:27.720 --> 00:06:29.755
-That's right.
Oh, beautiful.

00:06:29.755 --> 00:06:31.557
Bob Dylan, everybody!

00:06:31.557 --> 00:06:34.159
Can't believe
he took the time --

00:06:34.159 --> 00:06:36.261
I can't believe
he took the time to call us

00:06:36.261 --> 00:06:39.465
and to do an impersonation
of himself from 50 years ago.

00:06:39.465 --> 00:06:40.532
-[ Speaking indistinctly ]

00:06:40.532 --> 00:06:43.802
-Thank you, Bob.
[ Laughter ]

00:06:43.802 --> 00:06:46.072
-Well, guys, Christmas is just
a few weeks away,

00:06:46.072 --> 00:06:48.774
and I saw that the world's
first ever commercially printed

00:06:48.774 --> 00:06:52.578
Christmas card
is on sale for $25,000.

00:06:52.578 --> 00:06:54.913
Yeah, even back then, the first
person to get a Christmas card

00:06:54.913 --> 00:06:56.983
was like, "Wow. He gained
a lot of weight this year."

00:06:56.983 --> 00:06:58.917
[ Laughter ]

00:06:58.917 --> 00:07:01.253
Here's a big sports story.
The New York Jets

00:07:01.253 --> 00:07:05.190
are still looking for their
first win of the season.

00:07:05.190 --> 00:07:07.894
And yesterday,
they were up by 4

00:07:07.894 --> 00:07:10.897
with about 10 seconds
left in the game.

00:07:10.897 --> 00:07:13.665
All they had to do was
not give up a touchdown.

00:07:13.665 --> 00:07:15.701
Let's see how it went.

00:07:18.671 --> 00:07:20.306
-Jets coming.

00:07:20.306 --> 00:07:22.308
Carr puts some air under it.

00:07:22.308 --> 00:07:25.044
Wide open is Ruggs
for the touchdown!

00:07:25.044 --> 00:07:29.381
[ Laughter ]

00:07:29.381 --> 00:07:32.285
-The Jets are always
out-Jetting themselves.

00:07:32.285 --> 00:07:33.952
[ Laughter ]

00:07:33.952 --> 00:07:36.689
They're basically the NFL's
version of Rudy Giuliani.

00:07:36.689 --> 00:07:37.857
[ Laughter ]

00:07:37.857 --> 00:07:39.958
And, finally, every day,
we learn a little more

00:07:39.958 --> 00:07:42.361
about the coronavirus,
and now a doctor is warning

00:07:42.361 --> 00:07:46.098
that COVID could actually cause
erectile dysfunction.

00:07:46.098 --> 00:07:48.567
So between their COVID vaccine
and Viagra,

00:07:48.567 --> 00:07:50.603
Pfizer's about to make it rain.

00:07:50.603 --> 00:07:53.772
We have exactly 10 shows left
before we go on Christmas break,

00:07:53.772 --> 00:07:55.173
which means it's time
for that beloved

00:07:55.173 --> 00:07:56.375
"Tonight Show" tradition.

00:07:56.375 --> 00:07:58.778
It's time for 12 Days
of Christmas Sweaters!

00:07:58.778 --> 00:08:00.312
Here we go!

00:08:00.312 --> 00:08:02.815
♪ 12 Days
of Christmas Sweaters ♪

00:08:02.815 --> 00:08:06.585
♪ 10 todays left ♪

00:08:06.585 --> 00:08:09.788
-That's right. Every show
between now and Christmas

00:08:09.788 --> 00:08:12.224
we'll be giving
one lucky audience member

00:08:12.224 --> 00:08:14.459
an exquisite Christmas sweater

00:08:14.459 --> 00:08:16.395
from the Countdown
to Christmas Cabinet.

00:08:16.395 --> 00:08:18.931
Now, since there
are 10 shows left,

00:08:18.931 --> 00:08:21.733
let's open door number 10.

00:08:21.733 --> 00:08:23.436
Go for it.

00:08:23.436 --> 00:08:26.272
Oh, yeah.
Yes.

00:08:26.272 --> 00:08:28.674
Oh, yeah.

00:08:28.674 --> 00:08:30.676
Ooh, la, la!

00:08:30.676 --> 00:08:32.845
Couple gingerbread men.

00:08:32.845 --> 00:08:34.580
Look at that.

00:08:34.580 --> 00:08:37.949
Oh. Wow!
Wow. There are gloves.

00:08:37.949 --> 00:08:39.785
Looks like
the gloves are attached.

00:08:39.785 --> 00:08:42.221
Are there gl--
There are gloves attached.

00:08:42.221 --> 00:08:46.091
Wow. And let's see the back
just to check out the, uh...

00:08:46.091 --> 00:08:48.928
Yep, yep. Secret wreath,
not quite in the middle,

00:08:48.928 --> 00:08:51.496
off to the side a little bit,
kind of keeps you guessing.

00:08:51.496 --> 00:08:52.865
All right, everybody.

00:08:52.865 --> 00:08:54.600
Let's see who's gonna go home
with tonight's sweater.

00:08:54.600 --> 00:08:56.035
Everyone,
look at your seat number.

00:08:56.035 --> 00:08:58.237
If I call your number,
come on down.

00:08:58.237 --> 00:09:00.272
Quest, can I get
a drumroll, please?

00:09:00.272 --> 00:09:02.308
[ Drumroll ]

00:09:02.308 --> 00:09:03.743
Here we go.

00:09:03.743 --> 00:09:06.545
Number 260!

00:09:06.545 --> 00:09:07.980
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:09:07.980 --> 00:09:10.683
Come on down, bud!

00:09:10.683 --> 00:09:15.354
♪♪

00:09:15.354 --> 00:09:17.623
-Hello!

00:09:17.623 --> 00:09:19.825
Hello. What is your name
and where are you from?

00:09:19.825 --> 00:09:21.227
-Ethan.
I'm from New Jersey.

00:09:21.227 --> 00:09:23.062
-Hey!
New Jersey in the house!

00:09:23.062 --> 00:09:24.597
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:09:24.597 --> 00:09:28.167
It does get a little brisk
in New Jersey this time of year.

00:09:28.167 --> 00:09:30.402
Do you have anything like this
type of sweater?

00:09:30.402 --> 00:09:33.372
-Uh, not really.
[ Laughter ]

00:09:33.372 --> 00:09:35.340
-Not really. Would you mind
trying it on for us?

00:09:35.340 --> 00:09:36.675
-Sure.
-Roots, could we get some

00:09:36.675 --> 00:09:38.210
trying-on music?

00:09:38.210 --> 00:09:39.211
♪♪

00:09:39.211 --> 00:09:41.781
Thank you very much.

00:09:41.781 --> 00:09:43.816
Yeah, make sure
you get the fingers there.

00:09:43.816 --> 00:09:45.584
[ Laughter ]

00:09:45.584 --> 00:09:47.853
It's not something you want
to put on if you're in a rush.

00:09:47.853 --> 00:09:50.789
You know, you want to take
your time with this one.

00:09:50.789 --> 00:09:54.359
Man, it feels warm already.
Yep.

00:09:54.359 --> 00:09:57.496
Little tricky,
but that's half the fun of it.

00:09:57.496 --> 00:10:00.365
Oh!
Oh, yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:10:00.365 --> 00:10:02.134
Oh.
Oh, look at this.

00:10:02.134 --> 00:10:03.502
[ Cheers and applause ]
Look at that.

00:10:03.502 --> 00:10:05.204
Turn around.
Let's see the full --

00:10:05.204 --> 00:10:07.606
Yeah!
Looks like a tassel.

00:10:07.606 --> 00:10:08.941
[ Laughs ]

00:10:08.941 --> 00:10:10.543
Looks like you got, like,
a rattail in the back.

00:10:10.543 --> 00:10:12.011
I think it's pretty awesome.

00:10:12.011 --> 00:10:14.246
That's what I'm talking about.
That's our winner right there.

00:10:14.246 --> 00:10:16.348
That's our audience member.
We love you.

00:10:16.348 --> 00:10:17.950
Thank you again
to our lucky audience member.

00:10:17.950 --> 00:10:19.518
Stick around.
We'll be right back

00:10:19.518 --> 00:10:21.153
with more "Tonight Show,"
everybody.

00:10:21.153 --> 00:10:22.654
Come on back.

00:10:22.654 --> 00:10:29.762
♪♪

